  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run (6 witnesses, 4 names, composes nothing), so I used 1 of the 6 runs.\n\n**Rule** (`LVMC_11_40_180_A.lean`):\n- **Who it covers (a2):** a road user that is a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter, each written as its admitted aggregate with the aggregate id as the argument.\n- **When it applies (a3, a4):** the subject occupies a region of kind `sidewalk`, and the Fremont Street (Main to Seventh) assumption holds. I wrote the sidewalk claim as the region kind because `st_sidewalk` isn't an atom a formula can call.\n- **What it requires (a1):** the subject is at rest, using `drv_motion_complete_halt` with `p.halt_speed_tolerance`.\n- **a5** (the sign posting) stays a residue and isn't written.\n- I made no reading of my own, so `narrowings` is empty.\n\n**Witnesses:** the sidewalk runs beside the roadway, and the bicycle either moves at 4 m/s (40 times the 0.1 m/s tolerance) or stands at 0 m/s.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | bicycle moving on the sidewalk inside the stretch | violated |\n| `permit` | bicycle at rest on the sidewalk | compliant |\n| `idle` | bicycle moving on the roadway, not the sidewalk | not applicable |\n| `blind` | bicycle on the sidewalk with no speed reported | unknown |\n| `branch_1` | bicycle moving on a sidewalk outside the stretch | not applicable |\n| `branch_2` (added) | electric bicycle moving on the sidewalk | violated |\n\nI added `branch_2` so the electric-bicycle class is tested.\n\nUnder this run's reading, the electric-scooter aggregate includes no class, so it can only ever be unknown or false. No witness can show a scooter decided as violating or complying. That matches the node's stated intent, because the scooter's weight, top speed and purpose aren't observed.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
